## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, compliant telemetry pipeline with region isolation and real-time processing. It probes data modeling, idempotent semantics, and resilience at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Regional Pub/Sub and Dataflow streaming
- Schema validation and deduplication
- Tenant isolation via separate datasets and buckets
- Data residency and cross-region backups
- Observability and failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow transform sketch
function process(event) {
  if (!validateSchema(event)) throw new Error('Invalid');
  if (isDuplicate(event)) return;
  if (isAnomalous(event)) emit('anomaly', event);
  emitAggregates(event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you allocate costs per tenant?
- How would you test end-to-end failover in a CI pipeline?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect true cross-project isolation with scalable tenant onboarding, plus governance controls across storage, analytics, and metadata systems.

## Key Concepts
- IAM conditions and per-tenant service accounts
- Tenant-specific data planes (GCS prefixes, BigQuery datasets)
- Private Service Connect and VPC Service Controls for restricted egress
- Data Catalog/Dataplex as a data governance layer
- Dataflow/Test hooks for ingestion, auditing, rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-config: per-tenant IAM condition binding (conceptual)
{
  "binding": {
    "members": ["serviceAccount:tenant-123@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com"],
    "role": "roles/bigquery.dataViewer",
    "condition": {
      "title": "Tenant-specific dataset access",
      "expression": "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/datasets/tenant_123_')"
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical GCP design for multi-tenant data isolation, basic automation, and security without overengineering.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant data isolation with BigQuery datasets
- On-demand provisioning via Cloud Functions
- Least-privilege IAM per tenant and Authorized Views
- Cost control using quotas/labels and dataset partitioning
- Rollback path: revoke access and delete resources

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo provisioning sketch
if (newTenant) {
  createDataset(tenantId);
  bootstrapSchema(tenantId);
  createServiceAccount(tenantId);
  grantAccess(tenantSA, dataset);
  createAuthorizedView(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle schema evolution across tenants?
- How would you monitor per-tenant quotas and alert when nearing limits?
